<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # 1 – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 2nd Grade (CEFR: Pre-A1.4)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Fun Outdoors!</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> I Love to Run!</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Follow two-step spoken instructions related to classroom activities. Interactive: Retell a simple instruction or message accurately to another peer.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can follow two-step instructions related to classroom outdoor activities (e.g., "Run to the corner and pick up the ball."). Can listen to simple instructions and retell them to a peer (e.g., "Pass the ball and jump three times."). Can get the gist of a 2-line conversation (e.g., "Do you want to play soccer, Maria?" "Yes, I love soccer").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 34%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-weight: bold;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification. Activate prior knowledge and introduce the theme.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher leads a "Simon Says" game using actions related to outdoor activities. "Simon says: run fast!" "Simon says: jump high!" "Simon says: play with a ball!" The teacher uses TPR to model each action. </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher introduces new vocabulary using large, colorful flashcards (e.g., 'run', 'jump', 'play', 'ball', 'park', 'friend'). For each word, the teacher shows the flashcard, says the word clearly, and performs the action with TPR. The teacher models the pronunciation of /r/ in "run" and /s/ in "swim" (e.g., "R-r-run!", "S-s-swim!") and emphasizes initial sounds (G /g/ for "game"). The teacher states "I love to run!" and points to a running image.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding using simple questions and actions for 2nd Grade / Pre-A1.4 learners.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Teacher shows 'jump' flashcard) "Am I running or jumping?" (Teacher performs a jump). Students respond chorally "Jumping!"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Teacher shows 'fast' flashcard and runs in place slowly, then fast) "Is this fast or slow?" (pointing to the fast action). Students respond chorally "Fast!"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-weight: bold;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Fun Outdoors!".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Short audio monologue (recorded by the teacher or a simple sound clip) about outdoor activities. Illustrated large picture showing children playing in a park (running, jumping, playing with a ball).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Audio script example:</b> "Hello, everyone! I love to play outside in the park. I run fast with my friend. We play with a big ball. My friend jumps high! It is so much fun! Do you like to play outside?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> The learner can get the gist of a 2-line conversation or short spoken message related to outdoor activities. Expressing preferences (listening to "I love to play outside.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (Listening for gist and specific details):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question:</b> The teacher plays the audio. "What does the person love to do? Play outside or read a book?" (Students point to the large park picture or say "Play outside!").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False (Visual Check):</b> The teacher plays the audio again, pausing. "Does the person run fast?" (Students nod Yes/No or give thumbs up/down). "Do they play with a small ball?" (Students respond based on the picture and audio).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Matching (Picture to Sound):</b> The teacher plays segments of the audio (e.g., "I run fast!") and students point to the child running in the large picture. Similarly for "jumps high" and "play with a ball."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-weight: bold;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Listening. Guided practice of target language.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Listening to follow simple instructions. Target grammar: Subject + verb + adverb ("I run fast."), Present simple ("I love to run."). Vocabulary: run, jump, play, fast, slow, ball, friend, park, love, like, fun. Pronunciation: /r/, /s/, G /g/.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Listen and Point (Controlled Practice):</b> The teacher displays flashcards of 'run fast', 'jump high', 'play ball', 'swim slowly'. The teacher says a phrase (e.g., "Run fast!"), and students listen and point to the correct flashcard. This is repeated several times with different phrases and speeds.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Listen and Act (Semi-controlled Drill):</b> The teacher gives one-step and simple two-step instructions, and students perform the actions using TPR. Examples: "Run!" "Jump!" "Play with a ball!" "Run fast!" "Jump slowly!" "Touch your nose and jump!" "Clap your hands and run slowly!" The teacher monitors and repeats for clarity, emphasizing /r/ and /s/ sounds.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Listen, Retell, and Act (Pair Interaction/Peer Check):</b> Students work in pairs. The teacher gives a simple two-step instruction to Student A (e.g., "Student A, pass the ball and jump three times."). Student A listens, retells the instruction to Student B, and Student B performs the actions. Then roles are swapped with a new instruction. This focuses on interactive listening and retelling.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">12-15 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-weight: bold;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Fun Outdoors!".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> "Listen and Play Outdoors!" game (role-play simulation of outdoor activities in the classroom).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b> The teacher leads a "Follow the Instructions" game based on outdoor scenarios. The teacher gives sequential two-step instructions for students to follow. The goal is for students to actively listen and respond physically to the instructions, simulating playing outdoors.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Imagine we are in the park! Run to the corner and pick up the red ball!" (Students run to a designated corner and mime picking up a ball).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Now, pass the ball to your friend and jump two times!" (Students mime passing and jumping).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Walk slowly to the door and then run fast back to your seat!"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do you like to play soccer, Maria?" (Teacher points to a student, Maria). "Yes, I love soccer!" (Maria replies). Then, "Kick the ball and clap your hands!"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in listening comprehension, collaborative interaction by following instructions as a group, and communicative task completion by successfully performing the two-step actions.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-weight: bold;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy to check learning and application.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> The teacher gives 3 new two-step instructions. Students listen and perform the actions individually or in small groups. For example:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Touch your head and then jump high two times."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Run to the window and stand still."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Clap your hands and then sit down slowly."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible physical response (student correctly follows both steps of the instruction).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Engagement and attentiveness to spoken instructions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity in performing the actions (e.g., distinguishing fast/slow).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer with thumbs up/down or by coloring a happy/sad face on a simple worksheet.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can I follow two instructions?" (Picture of a child following two steps).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is listening to instructions easy?" (Happy face / Sad face options).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-weight: bold;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Review of the lesson and planning for future learning.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What outdoor activity do you like best? (Run / Jump / Play with a ball)" (Students point to pictures).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Was it fun to listen and play today?" (Students respond yes/no or show a happy/neutral/sad face).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What aspects of the lesson worked well for the students (e.g., TPR, flashcards, partner activities)?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for students who struggled with following two-step instructions (e.g., more repetition, visual cues, slower pace)?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Were the pronunciation points (/r/, /s/) adequately addressed and practiced?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> "Great job listening today, everyone! Next time, we will look at some pictures and read a short story about friends playing outside. We will see the words 'run' and 'jump' in a book!"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>